    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a condensed starting core, as several key contributors, including **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson**, are sidelined by team off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining on the IL, we are leaning heavily on **Kyle Tucker** to carry the offensive load. **Kyle Tucker** earns our highest efficiency score of the day at 61.84; despite facing a lefty in Kerr, his elite profile sustains his value, and he remains our most reliable asset for maintaining category pacing in a matchup that otherwise lacks high-ceiling environments.\n\nThe remainder of our lineup sits in the marginal-to-strong transition zone. **Andy Pages** (53.60) and **Jackson Merrill** (49.86) provide essential stability. **Jackson Merrill** is a particularly interesting case; while his score is dragged down by the 3.14 xERA of Henderson, his 40% SB potential keeps him in the daily mix, as we continue to aggressively weight speed in accordance with our 5x5 Roto requirements. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out the starters at 47.90; while leading off is a massive boon for his plate appearance volume, the matchup against Snell acts as a significant headwind, suppressing his overall output potential.\n\nRegarding our bench, the decision-making process was limited by the lack of available games for depth pieces like **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, and **Coby Mayo**, all of whom are currently inactive due to scheduling. Consequently, no bench player truly challenged the starting four for a roster spot today. We are monitoring the status of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Nasim Nunez** as potential mid-week pivots, but given the current board, we are prioritizing the health of our game caps over chasing low-probability ceiling games from our reserves like **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, or **Curtis Mead**. We remain cautious, as no player in today's lineup carries a \"safe\" tag against their respective pitching matchups.",
